Ilkyne is a terrestrial planet like [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]] -- albeit slightly larger. It has much harsher weather patterns than most of Althane and is covered near-completely in dense cloud cover, making mapping the surface remotely impossible. Bursts of red lightning can be seen within the clouds, and a great shadow can sometimes be seen moving on the surface.

Beneath the cloud lies the City of Yellow, the seat of [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|the Deep]]. It is built as concentric rings around a hill, under a cover of yellow and red cloud that rarely parts. Any one part of the city looks right, but the parts just past the centre of the eye do not fit together, and each part seems more rigid when looked at directly than when not. A depression at the hill's top holds a lake of water so deep a blue it is nearly black, and in the middle of that lake stands a lighthouse.

The streets are paved in interlocking triangles, squares and hexagons, split by fissures that leak yellow light. The buildings are faced in stone like marble and roofed in gold tiles, and they bend and sag and drip as if half-melted, walls compressing in one place and stretching in another. The air is dry and acrid and smells of rotten eggs, and a low drone runs under everything. The sky overhead is a crowded starscape of deep blues and purples, cloudless and full of constellations no one on Althane knows, unlike the cloud cover seen from orbit. Hunched figures wrapped in yellow burlap shuffle through the streets, scratching at the walls and pointing at strangers, each trailing a cord that leads up toward the hill.

Six black pyramids stand spaced around the foot of the hill, their faces carved with spiralling yellow cracks, each with a plaque that names it in a script a reader understands without having learned it: Origin, Sky, Cycle, Geometry, History and Hierarchy. None of them shows a door.
